From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] CryCommon: gate int64/uint64 typedefs behind O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT for libtiff 4.5+ compat

libtiff 4.5+ (Fedora 44+) defines `int64` / `uint64` in <tiff.h>
(lines 88-89 on F44's libtiff 4.7.1) as `int64_t` / `uint64_t` —
equivalent to `long` / `unsigned long` on LP64. CryCommon's
BaseTypes.h defines them as `slonglong` / `ulonglong` (= `long
long` / `unsigned long long`). Same 64-bit width but C++ treats
`long` and `long long` as distinct types, so any TU including
both BaseTypes.h and tiffio.h fails to compile:

    /usr/include/tiff.h:88:37: error: typedef redefinition with
        different types ('int64_t' (aka 'long') vs 'slonglong'
        (aka 'long long'))

Patch0007 already migrated `uint8`/`uint16`/`uint32` deprecation
warnings in TIFFLoader.cpp + ImageTIF.cpp. This patch addresses
the int64/uint64 typedef collision, which is in a separate layer
of <tiff.h> and not addressable by the same C99-rename approach
(BaseTypes.h's int64/uint64 are foundational engine typedefs used
across hundreds of files; renaming them upstream-wide is out of
scope for the Fedora packaging track).

Approach: a guard macro `O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT`. The two
TIFF-using `.cpp` files (`Code/Editor/Util/ImageTIF.cpp` and
`Gems/Atom/Asset/ImageProcessingAtom/.../TIFFLoader.cpp`) define
this macro before any #includes. CryCommon's BaseTypes.h checks
for it and skips the int64/uint64 typedefs when set — letting
libtiff's typedefs win in those two TUs. The `sint64` typedef
(no libtiff equivalent) stays unconditional.

`SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION` on both `.cpp` files (in the two
relevant `CMakeLists.txt` files) keeps the macro scoped to a
single TU. Without this, CMake's unity-build merge would pull
the two TIFF files into a merge group with other `.cpp` files
that use CryCommon's int64/uint64, and those files would fail
to compile against the suppressed typedefs.

Bundled-libtiff builds (the default everywhere except Fedora's
`--with system_tiff`) don't define the macro and behavior is
unchanged. Only fires when system libtiff is in use.

Carry locally; not pitched to upstream. The proper upstream
fix would be migrating CryCommon to C99 typedefs (Option B of
the deferred-tiff analysis), which would touch overload
resolution, printf format specifiers, and template
specializations across the engine — out of scope for this
packaging-track patch. The guard is conservative: it changes
behavior only when explicitly opted into.

Path-anchored at the typedef declarations themselves and the
`ly_add_target` invocations so future upstream rebases are
unlikely to drift the hunk anchors.

Signed-off-by: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
---
--- a/Code/Legacy/CryCommon/BaseTypes.h
+++ b/Code/Legacy/CryCommon/BaseTypes.h
@@ -60,13 +60,23 @@
 static_assert(sizeof(uint32) == 4);
 static_assert(sizeof(sint32) == 4);
 
+// O3DE-Fedora-packaging: when O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT is defined (in the
+// TIFF .cpp files only), suppress the int64/uint64 typedefs so libtiff's
+// <tiff.h> typedefs can win in those TUs. CryCommon defines them as
+// slonglong/ulonglong (= long long); libtiff defines them as int64_t/uint64_t
+// (= long on LP64). Same width, distinct C++ types — typedef redefinition
+// error otherwise. See sources/0008-system-libtiff-compat.patch.
+#if !defined(O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT)
 typedef slonglong int64;
+#endif
 
 #ifndef O3DE_INT64_DEFINED
 #define O3DE_INT64_DEFINED
 typedef slonglong sint64;
+#if !defined(O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT)
 typedef ulonglong uint64;
 static_assert(sizeof(uint64) == 8);
+#endif
 static_assert(sizeof(sint64) == 8);
 #endif
 
--- a/Code/Editor/Util/ImageTIF.cpp
+++ b/Code/Editor/Util/ImageTIF.cpp
@@ -6,6 +6,11 @@
  *
  */
 
+// O3DE-Fedora-packaging: gate CryCommon's int64/uint64 typedefs (BaseTypes.h)
+// off so libtiff's <tiff.h> typedefs (int64_t/uint64_t) win in this TU.
+// SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION on this file (Code/Editor/CMakeLists.txt) keeps
+// the macro from leaking into the unity merge group.
+#define O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT 1
 
 #include "EditorDefs.h"
 
--- a/Gems/Atom/Asset/ImageProcessingAtom/Code/Source/ImageLoader/TIFFLoader.cpp
+++ b/Gems/Atom/Asset/ImageProcessingAtom/Code/Source/ImageLoader/TIFFLoader.cpp
@@ -6,6 +6,11 @@
  *
  */
 
+// O3DE-Fedora-packaging: gate CryCommon's int64/uint64 typedefs (BaseTypes.h)
+// off so libtiff's <tiff.h> typedefs (int64_t/uint64_t) win in this TU.
+// SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION on this file (Atom Code/CMakeLists.txt) keeps
+// the macro from leaking into the unity merge group.
+#define O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT 1
 
 #include <AzCore/Debug/Trace.h>
 #include <AzCore/Math/MathUtils.h>
--- a/Code/Editor/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Code/Editor/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -69,6 +69,15 @@
 
 ly_get_pal_tool_dirs(pal_tool_dirs ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/Platform)
 
+# O3DE-Fedora-packaging: ImageTIF.cpp defines O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT to
+# suppress CryCommon's int64/uint64 typedefs so libtiff's <tiff.h> typedefs
+# can win in that TU. SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION isolates the macro to a
+# single TU; without this, other .cpp files in the unity merge group that
+# use CryCommon's int64/uint64 would fail to compile against the suppressed
+# typedefs. See sources/0008-system-libtiff-compat.patch.
+set_source_files_properties(Util/ImageTIF.cpp
+    PROPERTIES SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION TRUE)
+
 ly_add_target(
     NAME EditorLib SHARED
     NAMESPACE Legacy
--- a/Gems/Atom/Asset/ImageProcessingAtom/Code/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Gems/Atom/Asset/ImageProcessingAtom/Code/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -36,6 +36,13 @@
 o3de_pal_dir(pal_source_dir ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/Source/Platform/${PAL_PLATFORM_NAME} "${gem_restricted_path}" "${gem_path}" "${gem_parent_relative_path}")
 set(common_source_dir ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/Source/Platform/Common)
 
+# O3DE-Fedora-packaging: TIFFLoader.cpp defines O3DE_SYSTEM_LIBTIFF_COMPAT to
+# suppress CryCommon's int64/uint64 typedefs so libtiff's <tiff.h> typedefs
+# can win in that TU. SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION isolates the macro to a
+# single TU. See sources/0008-system-libtiff-compat.patch.
+set_source_files_properties(Source/ImageLoader/TIFFLoader.cpp
+    PROPERTIES SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION TRUE)
+
 ly_add_target(
     NAME ${gem_name}.Editor.Static STATIC
     NAMESPACE Gem
